{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793709896,"nonce":"+RzmuTL79FrCswm+oC0townwNTU=","message":"Spinner under a Toast: root cause found and fixed in the working tree (uncommitted). Reproduced live in a small window (three spinners under a toast shown from a timer): only the rotating arcs drew over the toast. In the compositor's CSS-patch path, and in the full path, promoted CSS layers (composite_css_layers_overlay) and motion layers were composited AFTER dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay, which draws the overlay content (toast, popover). Main-tree layers therefore landed on top of overlay content; the static track stayed hidden because it is an ordinary primitive in the batch. Fix: DynamicRegion's ambient state records in_overlay_subtree; the composite steps take a LayerScope; main-tree layers composite before the dynamic batch and overlay-subtree layers after it, at all four call sites (three in compositor.rs, one in motion_rendering.rs). Checked live after the fix: the toast is clean. Not covered: promoted subtrees' text and SVG pools still dispatch after the batch. Headless does not reproduce it (the toast is not in the dynamic batch there), so there is no failing-first test; cn_progress_clip a_spinner_under_a_toast_* guard the headless path.","files":null}]}